{"book":11,"chapter":21,"rubric":"MODERN FRONTEND / CSS AND LAYOUT","slides":[{"title":"Responsive Design","sub":"One site, many screens","main":"Phone first; without the viewport meta tag a mobile browser shows the desktop version.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Screens","No viewport","With viewport","Meta tag"],"captions":["One page opens on a phone, a tablet and a big monitor, and must look good everywhere","Without the viewport meta tag a phone pretends to be a desktop: a thousand-pixel page is squeezed into the screen, the text is tiny","With the device width the page gets a real three hundred sixty pixels and the layout works as intended","The meta tag goes in the document head once, and without it the rest of responsive design does not work"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"d1","x":70.0,"y":80.0,"w":44.0,"h":76.0,"text":"phone","tone":"blue","size":8.0,"sub":"360px","sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d2","x":162.0,"y":80.0,"w":84.0,"h":60.0,"text":"tablet","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub":"768px","sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d3","x":280.0,"y":80.0,"w":130.0,"h":80.0,"text":"monitor","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub":"1440px","sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":152.0,"text":"one page, many screens","size":10.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"d1","x":90.0,"y":82.0,"w":80.0,"h":120.0,"text":"","tone":"blue","size":8.0,"sub":"screen 360px","sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"q","x":90.0,"y":82.0,"w":68.0,"h":70.0,"text":"page\n980px\nshrunk","tone":"red","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n1","x":250.0,"y":70.0,"text":"text is tiny,","tone":"red","size":10.0},{"t":"text","id":"n2","x":250.0,"y":88.0,"text":"you have to pinch","tone":"red","size":10.0},{"t":"text","id":"n3","x":250.0,"y":106.0,"text":"with fingers","tone":"red","size":10.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"d1","x":90.0,"y":82.0,"w":80.0,"h":120.0,"text":"","tone":"blue","size":8.0,"sub":"screen 360px","sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"q","x":90.0,"y":82.0,"w":68.0,"h":70.0,"text":"page\n360px\nas 